            "text": "{\"description\":\"The visible stone surface shows a large carved human-like torso or head-and-body form with a prominent face-like area: two deep oval depressions, a raised circular element below them, and broad curved incised bands beneath. The upper part has worn vertical and curved incisions, including smaller face-like or body-like relief details, but many lines are shallow and eroded.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"I do not see a clear carved bird or birdlike head/beak on the main stone surface; the bird shapes at the right are background objects, not carving on the stone.\",\"box\":null},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A large face-like arrangement is visible on the main front surface, with two deep eye-like oval depressions and a central raised circular feature, occupying much of the upper front of the lower stone body.\",\"box\":[0.18,0.4,0.74,0.68]},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No carved form with multiple legs and a segmented upturned tail is visible on the stone surface.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"There is a distinct raised circular motif below the two oval depressions on the front surface; it is separate from an eye or nostril.\",\"box\":[0.393,0.544,0.545,0.636]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"I do not see three repeated arch-topped forms arranged side by side in a row; the curved bands are long arcs, not three separate arch forms.\",\"box\":null},\"limitations\":\"The stone is rough, dark, and heavily worn, with shallow eroded lines and uneven lighting that make some upper carvings difficult to read.\"}",
